phases = []
def phase(n,title,finding,evidence,table=None):
    phases.append(dict(phase=n,title=title,finding=finding,evidence=[E[x] for x in evidence],table=table))

phase(0,'Baseline / freeze',f'Initial shell observation: clean main at {BASELINE["head"]}, VERSION 0.12.1, empty diff stat. The later freeze-time status includes only the newly created audit directory. Criteria were locked before evaluation; SHA256 {LOCK_SHA}. All 3,217 tracked files are hashed, with backend/frontend/science/policy/persistence/OpenAPI/docs/VERSION group identities. No production writes are authorized. Historical shipping-source comparison matches 82/82 source identities; toolchain/dependency/frontend/docs changes do not certify a new resource envelope.',['shipping'], 'source_groups')
phase(1,'Define the product in one sentence','A.T.O.M is a local-first, open-source workspace for comparing small urban cellular-network configurations on real maps using deterministic RF planning estimates and bounded azimuth search. README, docs, app and Product Compass share this thesis. README engine language and acronym density are more technical than necessary; first useful decision is less prominent than features. Git remote identifies Berk-Unsal/atom; no GitHub About description was present in the inspected tracked metadata, and live GitHub metadata was not fetched.',['readme','landing','compass','product'])
phase(2,'Actual users','Primary users are engineers making bounded comparisons and telecom learners/researchers inspecting assumptions; experimenters, systems engineers and contributors are secondary. Evidence supports no operator/enterprise workflow claim. Personas below distinguish supported jobs from reasonable unmet expectations.',['readme','compass','features'],'personas')
phase(3,'Use-case clarity','The defensible job is comparing a small configured urban plan, seeing trade-offs, explaining a recommendation and preserving evidence. Supported uses are classified below. The supplied “what is the use case?” comment is a product-clarity signal only. A broad capabilities catalogue answers what the software contains better than why a newcomer should perform its first comparison.',['readme_features','guide','tools'],'use_cases')
phase(4,'First 30 seconds','Heuristic inspection, not a timed user study: the fresh live app shows Telecom planning, a single Cell,5G / 28 GHz, UMa model, Run needed, a visible Run Sector action, Setup and four stages. A newcomer can identify a map-based RF tool and first compute action; intended decision, source data certainty and accuracy boundary are less visible until disclosures/Data/docs. README identifies engineers/students and estimates; docs hero says inspect/run/model before a user outcome. A simulator/planner/optimizer combination is discoverable but not yet one crisp first-use promise.',['chrome','setup','landing','readme'])
phase(5,'End-to-end workflow','The primary loop is intentional and connected. Trace below combines current source, regression/browser checks and retained historical real eight-Cell F28 evidence. The present browser workflow suites use mocked APIs; Go tests exercise real engine/controlled geometry; live inspection used the full Ankara backend only for first-screen/navigation observation. This audit did not rerun the costly frozen operational matrix or claim a fresh real-backend eight-Cell browser qualification. Dead ends are local and explicit: no retained Version for Apply, unsupported 140 GHz analyses, independent tool caps, deadlines and export guards.',['guide','e2e','cap_tests','promotion'],'workflow')
phase(6,'Tool information architecture','Four stages and task-specific progressive disclosures provide real hierarchy; major capabilities are not all permanent peers. Core Lab and deep references can distract when discovered without a planning question, but their optional/isolated scope is valuable and not grounds for deletion. Data carries both source provenance and measurement experiments; Results has several meanings. Preserve current hierarchy and teach the core route before considering new navigation.',['tools','features'],'tools')
phase(7,'Terminology','Cell is the selected RF record; tower is a legacy/API/data alias; sector is a directional configuration; site is contextual, not verified infrastructure. These must not be normalized by assumption. Coverage may mean ray reach, building service or sampled surface; optimization changes azimuth, and optimal is bounded. RF profile, Profile A and Auto have distinct meanings. Terminology inventory follows.',['guide','api_optimal','limits','tools'],'terms')
phase(8,'Scientific claim inventory','The atomic claim matrix below assigns exactly one A–F primary level to each of 56 claim families. The lexical appendix inventories 3,330 matching textual occurrences in 184 files, including generated duplicates and historical reports; validation of input/schema or software is not RF accuracy. Historical qualification/design claims remain attributed to their original scope, never rewritten as present product guarantees. Standards basis is traced to current implementation/citations/fixtures; this is not an independent standards-conformance certification.',['limits','reference_tests','promotion'],'claims')
phase(9,'RF model boundaries','2.6/28 GHz use the deterministic outdoor UMa path-loss subset with height-aware centerline LOS/NLOS and explicit legacy fallback. Unknown roof evidence is conservative NLOS. Urban NLOS does not get an extra legacy wall penalty.140 GHz is a research attenuation profile with isolated standards references, not canonical radio quality. Building entry is a representative zero-depth facade estimate. Antennas are analytic/single-element references, receiver assumptions scalar/manual or derived. Terrain is optional path-profile evidence and absent from canonical fast RF. Main detailed limits are sound; the landing FSPL/walls summary is stale.',['algorithms','rf','limits','landing_default'])
phase(10,'Measurement-validation status','The current sanitized real-pilot readiness says real_data_ingested_validation_blocked: 53,005 raw data rows parsed, zero malformed/dropped samples, 1,858 elapsed-order warnings, 83 registered-flag rows all with NONE connection status, 37 collector serving-change events, and zero canonical observations. Exact pack mapping is absent. B7 bandwidth/resource association, 2.665 versus 2.600 GHz, transmitter/receiver/LOS truth remain separate blockers. No canonical pilot residual artifact or defensible MAE/RMSE resulted. Ordinary CSV diagnostics, isolated research ledger and canonical campaign library are separate capabilities.',['pilot','pilot_note','canonical','measurement_ui'])
phase(11,'Model accuracy wording','Current main copy explicitly says planning estimate and excludes field/UE/PHY calibration. Accurate/precise language found in current overview material is chiefly a negated limit, future contribution example, coordinate precision or software/data validation. Dangerous exceptions: unconditional validated-sounding bias heading on an ineligible result; maximum-coverage/optimal sector prose; old unscoped parallelization timings. Verified RF follow-up refers to request authorization, not verified physical RF. Do not infer accuracy from standards citations, regression tests, hash equality or operating within resource budgets.',['readme','bias_heading','api_optimal','legacy_benchmark'])
phase(12,'Eight-Cell claim boundary','Normal network 8 is source/test/API behavior. Operational evidence is the exact frozen paired Ankara 2026.07 W1 layouts,2.6/28 GHz,120 rays / 400 m / 30 dBm / 120°, legacy two-pass, historical Go 1.26.6 Linux/arm64 Profile A 2 CPU/4 GiB. No W2/W3, arbitrary hardware/datasets, stronger models or multi-instance qualification follows. Current README explicitly states limits; no blanket arbitrary-eight certification was found. Current capability reference incorrectly understates the cap as 6.',['readme_scope','promotion','features_cap','cap_tests'])
phase(13,'Performance claims / causal attribution','Recorded affected six-Cell 28 GHz request: uncached 94.707–112.731 s; corrected same-container controls 6.720739/6.760776/6.749160 s.434 network proposals preserved;2,604 contribution requests reduced to 180 expensive misses with 2,424 hits. Five distinct profiles/locations among six IDs matter. Scheduling, workers and candidate parallelism were unchanged. The evidence isolates contribution reuse as the correction; no controlled factorial split quantifies caching versus all historical concurrency/other improvements. The supplied Reddit question prompts this check and is not proof.',['performance','cache','concurrency'])
phase(14,'Benchmark communication','Historical deadline report responsibly gives payload, band, rays, radius, toolchain, hardware, quotas, before/after, tiny samples and confounders. It measures admitted requests, not the complete user journey; map refresh, persistence and dataset load have separate cost. Request-local memoization is rebuilt per request, not a persistent cross-request warm cache. Whole-system cold/warm/runtime effects were not controlled enough to promise a universal number. Algorithms 36 s → 250 ms / 4× prose has none of the required context and is unsupported as a released benchmark. Profile A 11.788 s worst request and 1.217 GB kernel peak belong to the separate matrix, not this speedup comparison.',['performance','legacy_benchmark','promotion'])
phase(15,'Resource qualification','Profile A is a reference qualification, not a universal minimum system requirement. Frozen W1/paired layouts/settings, single-instance/Linux/arm64 cgroupv2/CGO0, historical Go 1.26.6, fixed concurrency 2/1,60 s deadline and worker 1 / queue 16 define the envelope. Recorded promotion worst request11.788444160 s, minimum headroom 48.211555840 s and process-lifetime kernel peak 1,217,204,224 bytes with no OOM/kill/max events are historical measurements. The current toolchain is 1.26.9; source equality and race tests do not requalify its resource/performance binary.',['promotion','shipping','readme_scope'])
phase(16,'Request-budget UX','20 ordinary attempts per ClientIP / anchored 60 s plus 8 shared verified eligible follow-up units enables the declared normal map/azimuth journeys without teaching capability accounting to users. Prebooking/fail-closed tests support avoiding budget-exhausted partial eligible fan-out, not guaranteeing all RF work succeeds. API docs should carry counters/headers, architecture docs ownership/verification details, UI the problem and wait/retry action. Current error text distinguishes capacity/budget, but Retry-After is only stored on Error and catches display message. NAT sharing and charged failures can surprise users; no automatic retry or admission redesign is recommended here.',['workflow_policy','api_budget','api_client','protection'])
phase(17,'Eight-Cell product limit UX','Setup shows selected count, minimum 2 / maximum 8 and refuses a ninth without RF. This feels intentional as a product limit, but the reason is mostly discoverable in README/qualification rather than at the point of selection. The useful explanation is a currently supported small-plan operational scope; users do not need W1/Profile A internals to select Cells. Eight is not a scientific law or guarantee of accuracy.',['cap_ui','readme_scope','cap_tests'])
phase(18,'Independent cap coherence','Normal 8, Recommendation existing-input 5, Measurement 1–6 are deliberately independent and remain unchanged. README current scope table is clear. Candidate UI guard/explanation uses 5 and requires a drawn area; app flow further requires at least 2 existing inputs although endpoint supports its own minimum. Measurement UI advertises 5,000 samples but not max 6 and its handler lacks a maximum precheck, so an eight-Cell user encounters a backend rejection. Document this as recoverable workflow debt, not an argument to equalize caps.',['readme_caps','recommendation_guard','measurement_handler','measurements'])
phase(19,'Results / explainability','Results answers what happened through scores/raw metrics; baseline impact and comparisons show compared with what; thresholds and conditional per-Cell effects show why; non-dominated Solutions support trade-offs. Is it good requires user priorities and policy context:64/100 is neither 64% coverage nor accuracy. Objective meanings and raw denominators are present but not automatically understood. Current empty/infeasible states avoid success claims. Next-inspection guidance exists per tool but is less unified than the evidence itself.',['results','goals','report_pareto','interference_ui'])
phase(20,'Optimization semantics','Default network search is deterministic two-pass coordinate azimuth search on 10° candidates;578 proposals for 8 Cells. Other radio/geometry inputs stay fixed. Priorities weight normalized available utilities, hard constraints gate feasibility; radio quality opt-in starts at 0. Opt-in multistart/archive searches are bounded heuristics. A retained Pareto set is discovered, truncated and not global; local priority reranking is not new RF search. UI/report recommendation wording is substantially honest; single-sector API optimal/max coverage sentence is overbroad and conflates weighted demand with coverage.',['api_bounded','cap_tests','goals','report_pareto','api_optimal'])
phase(21,'Uncertainty / provenance','Strong current principle: static source licenses/hashes, observed_tag vs levels-derived vs unknown roof evidence, requested/applied models, applicability/fallback, receiver/quality/building thresholds, Run/Version lineage and report hashes remain explicit. Data calls demand heuristic, not subscriber measurements. Unknown fields remain unsupported/missing rather than promoted. Absolute accuracy uncertainty is not quantified by deterministic repeatability; the real-pilot block is preserved. A report hash proves artifact integrity only.',['data_confidence','app_model','reports','pilot'])
phase(22,'Errors / empty states','Empty states suggest select Cells/run analysis/import samples; unsupported 140 GHz quality is explicit. Stale/historical result badges and unavailable Apply states preserve evidence boundaries. Cap errors and persistence errors are real failures, not success banners. Recovery gaps: Measurement 6 surfaces after submission, generic resource-budget export wording does not teach which artifact to reduce, and retry metadata is not translated into a wait. Browser/Go tests support representative paths; no exhaustive failure-mode or formal accessibility certification was performed.',['empty','interference_ui','apply','api_client','store_export'])
phase(23,'Report / export honesty','HTML and Markdown builders retain selected Cells, request/model/dataset/application metadata, source Runs/Versions, score/baseline/Pareto evidence and limitations. Reports say deterministic planning estimate, not measurement or deployment approval; scalar correction is not full calibration; conditional effects are noncausal. Missing data has explicit unavailable representation. Report maps sample rays for readability with disclosure; full result preservation belongs to bounded project/artifact storage, not the map image. Some exact identity/hash evidence is in retained artifact/source data rather than every printable summary. No claim of complete universal portable evidence is warranted.',['reports','report_limits','report_map','report_pareto','store_export'])
phase(24,'Persistence expectations','Known historical eight-Cell network-result-only round-trip is supported, and current regression suite preserves it.16 MiB file,250k encoded-node,32 MiB/1M decoded-content guards remain. Oversize export throws before download; this audit found no evidence that a rejected export is reported as safely exported. Only recent scenario layers are cached, older inputs remain and require rerun. Draft autosave, immutable Version and downloadable project are different promises. Current README caveat is honest, but discoverability/recovery remain medium debt.',['store','store_export','store_retention','promotion'])
phase(25,'README verdict','Good scoped technical introduction and strong scientific caveats; visible scope table, versioned gallery, LFS/Docker/readiness path, settings-first sample, limitations and contribution links. It primarily sells a large capability set after its overview, rather than leading with one concrete comparison problem/outcome. Screenshots demonstrate results/control density more than the complete first planning decision. Source-build/LFS friction is explicit and appropriate; no turnkey operator workflow is implied by the strongest caveats.',['readme','readme_caps','readme_gallery','readme_start'])
phase(26,'Docs landing verdict','Clear run locally CTA, one planning loop and a prominent confidence boundary lower on the page; search/navigation and light/dark behavior pass current browser checks. Architecture is a peer first destination, so internal system explanation competes with first user outcome. Default propagation sentence is stale, current capability link leads to a 2–6 understatement, and theme previews differ in UI generation. Appearance itself does not invalidate the hierarchy; matched content and a concrete first task matter more than another palette change.',['landing','landing_limits','landing_default','landing_light','features_cap'])
phase(27,'Screenshot story','Inspected all four README gallery images and both docs hero assets in place. Network workspace: selection/order, rays and map key. Propagation drawer: configure beam/radius/rays plus explicit Optimize. Optimization results:64.3/100, deltas, raw denominators and discovered trade-offs; no first-selection or full apply/export action. Single-sector: alternative simpler mode and research disclosures. They partially tell configure→analyze→optimize→understand, but start in populated states and omit the initial question/baseline/export decision. Light hero is an older UI capture; dark hero is the current eight-Cell workspace. Captions do not establish measured performance or accuracy.',['readme_gallery','landing_light'],'screenshots')
phase(28,'Public positioning','Primary label: deterministic urban RF planning and experimentation workspace. Secondary: cellular-network simulator (planning estimates), bounded azimuth optimization tool, geospatial RF visualization/explanation tool. Research/reference platform describes the optional specialist area. A universal network planner,6G validated simulator or commercial operator-planning replacement is not defensible. The small-scale urban focus is an asset to preserve.',['compass','readme','limits'])
phase(29,'Commercial-tool expectation gap','Table distinguishes present, partial, absent and explicitly out-of-scope capabilities. Inventory fields are not an operator integration, configured loading is not capacity, terrain diagnostics are not canonical terrain propagation, CSV ingestion is not field validation, and Core overlays are not mobility/handover prediction. These are expectation boundaries, not an automatic feature wishlist.',['features','limits','pilot'],'commercial')
phase(30,'External feedback synthesis','Only supplied summaries were used. No Reddit thread/author/date or statistically representative audience evidence was provided; none was fetched or invented. Caching question matches repository evidence, use-case question reinforces first-use review, smooth-map praise is preservation input, and small urban scope is source-supported. There are no attributable planner feature requests to justify a new specialist capability.',['performance','compass'],'feedback')
phase(31,'Product debt inventory','Thirteen evidence-backed items below separate claim/documentation drift, workflow discoverability, terms, persistence expectations and integration readiness. None authorizes implementation. Strict OpenAPI integration is blocked; local core planning is not shown to be broken. Field-accuracy and calibration promotion are separately blocked by scientific evidence, not a missing UI feature.',['openapi','features_cap','measurement_handler','store'],'findings')
phase(32,'Scientific debt inventory','Scientific debt is chiefly unusable measurement evidence and unknown transmitter/resource/receiver truth. Model applicability is explicit; canonical terrain absence and advanced channel/PHY omissions are declared scope limitations, not automatically defects. Do not turn synthetic tests, source identity or operational success into a measured accuracy result.',['pilot','canonical','limits'],'scientific_debt')
phase(33,'What not to build next','Do not promote 10/12 Cells: no demonstrated user decision blocked by 8, and current independent/persistence limits do not disappear with a cap increase. Do not expand W2/W3 or repeat infrastructure qualification by default: W1 evidence is adequate for the declared use and no broader demand case exists. Do not reopen adaptive admission: invalid estimator validation remains historical evidence and Auto stays observation-only. Do not add arbitrary RF models, universal terrain/clutter physics or an enterprise wishlist without applicability, data and user-task evidence. These are defer decisions, not claims such work can never matter.',['promotion','compass','resource','pilot'])
phase(34,'Ranked next-phase options','Four directions, ordered by current evidence and dependency readiness, appear below. Cost/risk are qualitative planning judgments, not estimated schedules. Scientific validation is high-value but externally blocked; a bounded first-decision initiative is immediately achievable using the existing product. No large RF/infrastructure task is selected merely because it is technically interesting.',['compass','pilot','readme_start'],'options')
phase(35,'Single recommendation','Choose exactly one initiative: one reproducible first planning decision. Frame one existing small urban baseline→azimuth recommendation→trade-off→evidence export task, with current scope/accuracy language and matching captures. A newcomer should understand what decision A.T.O.M supports and why its result is conditional. Keep the current product and models; this is not a redesign. The implementation task should also track the named claim-copy/API defects as explicit bounded follow-ups, not silently broaden this audit. Scientific validation remains a separately blocked future study.',['readme_start','compass','guide'])
phase(36,'Final claim matrix','The matrix is compact by atomic claim family, with source/wording, one category, support judgment, required qualification and recommended wording. Recommended wording is audit output only and has not been applied. Unsupported inferred claims are explicitly marked as absent/inferred rather than falsely attributed to current README.',['readme_scope','limits','performance'],'claims')
phase(37,'Product workflow scorecard','Ordinal 1–5 scores use the locked anchors. They are auditor judgments from source, tests and bounded visual observation, not measured usability percentages; no arithmetic overall score is manufactured.',['compass','guide','limits'],'scorecard')
phase(38,'Audit verdict','B — STRONG PRODUCT WITH POSITIONING / WORKFLOW DEBT. The core planning estimates, data/model provenance, reference isolation and bounded azimuth comparison form one defensible product. New users must infer the first decision and reconcile local copy/cap/terminology drift. F-level benchmark, optimal/bias phrasing and schema defects are explicit findings; they do not establish a widespread field-accuracy or universal-model claim in current main product messaging. Therefore A is too generous, C is not supported as the overall physical-claim verdict, D lacks a major disconnected/broken core loop, and E is unnecessary given available source/tests/frozen evidence. External readiness is conditional, not an unqualified release approval.',['readme','limits','pilot','tools','legacy_benchmark','openapi'])
phase(39,'No implementation / freeze','End at findings. VERSION stays 0.12.1; all original tracked source, scientific/policy/persistence files, historical evidence and release metadata remain hash-identical. No caps/models/worker/deadline/admission/search/Pareto/Auto changes, README rewrite, changelog edit, tag, release, commit or push. Only the requested Markdown/JSON report and audit support/evidence directory are created. No recommendation is implemented.',['policy','store','shipping'])

